1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,906
Introducing AWISU: autonomous warehouse inventory with a small unmanned aircraft.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:15,654
The proposed platform combines a lightweight flight controller and onboard computing, within a three kilogram takeoff limit.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:23,607
Side cameras read labels. Stereo and lidar support navigation. The rotating aircraft is a reference simulation asset.

4
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:31,498
First, aligned sensor observations build local geometry. Motion proceeds through a known-free corridor, with room to stop.

5
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:39,312
Both sides follow a continuous five-level sweep. Complete label images and corroborating reads update the inventory.

6
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:47,684
A missed label triggers local recovery: brake, approach the affected side, retry, and resume from the unfinished boundary.

7
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:55,700
Optical sampling sets the scan speed. The energy budget includes recovery and reserve; battery delivery still requires qualification.

8
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:05,266
The reference simulation follows a prescribed route, replayed seven times faster with synchronized external, side, and forward views.

9
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:16,174
At the aisle end, the aircraft climbs and reverses along the next level. The route continues without resetting to the starting position.

10
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:28,406
Left and right cameras share the same recorded aircraft pose. The inventory count is drawn from the original saved decoding records.

11
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:39,105
The lower panel traces the growing route and tracking error, while the side views show the labels passing through each camera.

12
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:50,138
The fifth pass completes the upper level. This experiment evaluates route tracking and barcode reading on the reference plant.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,502
After scanning, the aircraft returns along the aisle. It then descends and lands, completing the continuous flight.

14
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:15,178
Saved-image checks confirm four hundred identities. Tracking error improves by nine point six percent over the baseline.
